I'll inspect the activity wall and the data layer that feeds it.## 1. Review & Understand the Task

- **Target**: the "Latest activity" card `src/components/solopreneur/SolopreneurWall.vue` (used by the Solopreneur summary).
- **Requirement A – ticket name**: each activity row must say *which ticket* it refers to. Today it only shows author, relative time, kind badge, message text and a board/project chip.
- **Requirement B – live refresh**: the card loads its data once in `created()`; new/updated tickets never appear until a page reload.

## 2. Information Gathering

- A **ticket IS a chat** (`useSolopreneurProjects.js`: "a sprint/kanban card IS a chat"); the ticket title is `chat.name`, status is `chat.status`, board is `chat.board`/`chat.column`, recency is `chat.updated_at`.
- The card renders `buildPosts({ chats, meets })` from `wall/wallEvents.js`. The post object carries `chatId` but **not** the chat name → the title is lost at render time.
- Refresh signals already exist in the app:
  - `$storex.chats.allChats` (active project) — new chat objects are registered on create/update (`createNewChat`, `newSprintTask`, `saveChatInfo`).
  - `$storex.session.events` — socket events; `store/session.js` pushes `{ event, data, ts }` and `store/chats.js → onChatEvent` treats `data.chat` + `data.type === 'changed'` / `event_type === 'done'` as "chat document created/updated". This is the only signal for the *other* recent projects the card also reads.
- `loadChats()` fetches up to 3 projects, so a reload is the correct (and only) way to pick up tickets outside the active project.
- `load()` currently always sets `status = 'loading'` → a naive refresh would flash the skeleton every time a ticket moves.

## 3. Change Proposal

- Keep `this.chats` (`[{ chat, project }]`) as the single source and derive `chatNames` (id → title) from it; add `nameOf(post)` for the template.
- Render the ticket title as its own semibold line in the row (truncated, with `title` tooltip), suppressing it when it equals the message text (chat with no messages) to avoid duplication.
- Add two cheap change detectors + watchers (no deep watching):
  - `ticketSignature` — id/name/status/column/board/updated_at of the store chats (active project, covers create/rename/move/updates).
  - `ticketEventCount` — count of socket events that mean "chat document changed/done" (covers any project).
- Both call `scheduleRefresh()`: debounced (800 ms) **silent** reload that keeps the current feed on screen; in-flight requests are never stacked, and a silent failure keeps the last good data. Timer cleared in `beforeUnmount`.
- Risks: none functional — `wallEvents.js` / `Wall.vue` untouched; only this one component changes. Loop safety: the signature is derived from the store, not from the fetched list, so a reload does not re-trigger itself (verified against `loadChats()`, which only mutates local state and, at most once, the chats store).

